      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nThe XPU flash attention shim in `vllm/_xpu_ops.py` accepts `num_splits` and then\r\ndrops it: it is listed in the \"not used in xpu kernel currently\" block and never\r\nforwarded to `vllm_xpu_kernels.flash_attn_interface.flash_attn_varlen_func`. So\r\nthe `max_num_splits = 1` that `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT` sets in\r\n`vllm/v1/attention/backends/flash_attn.py` never reaches the kernel, which keeps\r\nchoosing its own split count via `get_num_splits()`. This PR forwards it as\r\n`num_splits_kv` and moves the parameter out of the stale comment block that made\r\nthe omission look deliberate.\r\n\r\nThe determinism suite could not catch this. `_random_prompt(10, 50)` in\r\n`tests/v1/determinism/utils.py` only pads when the target exceeds 50 words, so it\r\nreturns roughly 16 tokens: the KV of every request fits inside a single kernel\r\nblock and no backend has a split to be inconsistent about. This PR adds\r\n`_prompt_with_tokens(target_tokens)`, which tokenizes with the test model to hit\r\nan exact token count, and uses ~2k-token prompts in the bs=1 vs bs=N test.\r\n\r\nA residual violation survives this fix and is a **separate** defect, not\r\naddressed here: the XPU kernel serves decode (`max_seqlen_q == 1`) from\r\n`cutlass_paged_decode_interface` and prefill from\r\n`cutlass_chunk_prefill_interface`, and those two reduce over KV differently\r\n(the decode path has its own FP32 `max_logits`/`exp_sums` and a cross-sub-group\r\nSLM epilogue). A prefix-cache hit that leaves a single query token therefore\r\ndisagrees with the cold prefill whatever the split count is, so no argument to\r\nthis shim can align them. That belongs in `vllm-xpu-kernels`; XPU users who need\r\nbatch invariance should keep using `TRITON_ATTN`, as\r\n`docs/features/batch_invariance.md` already documents.\r\n\r\n## Why this is not a duplicate\r\n\r\n- #55881 also concerns XPU batch invariance but only touches\r\n  `vllm/platforms/xpu.py` backend selection; it does not touch\r\n  `vllm/_xpu_ops.py`, and the dropped `num_splits` is unfixed on `main`.\r\n- #55958 is the ROCm equivalent of the backend-selection change, not the shim.\r\n- `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search \"num_splits_kv\"`\r\n  returns nothing.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\nXPU (Intel(R) Arc(TM) Pro B70 Graphics, single card, `Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B`):\r\n\r\n- `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 VLLM_ATTENTION_BACKEND=FLASH_ATTN pytest -sq\r\n  tests/v1/determinism/test_batch_invariance.py::test_logprobs_bitwise_batch_invariance_bs1_vs_bsN`\r\n  with the longer prompts: 21-23 of 32 prompts mismatch before this change,\r\n  1-2 of 32 after it. (FLASH_ATTN has to be forced; it is not the batch-invariant\r\n  backend for XPU.)\r\n- `VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 pytest -sq\r\n  tests/v1/determinism/test_batch_invariance.py::test_decode_logprobs_match_prefill_logprobs`\r\n  on `TRITON_ATTN`: 1 passed in 151.18s.\r\n- Instrumented shim: all 364 kernel calls in a batch-invariant run now receive\r\n  `num_splits_kv=1`, including the 112 decode-shaped calls with\r\n  `max_seqlen_q=1`; the remaining decode-vs-prefill residual (~9e-02) is\r\n  reproducible and deterministic, which is what identifies it as the separate\r\n  kernel-side defect described above.\r\n\r\nCUDA (NVIDIA L40S, single card, vLLM 0.28.1rc1.dev609+gc69d5d72a):\r\n`VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 pytest -sq ...::test_logprobs_bitwise_batch_invariance_bs1_vs_bsN`\r\npasses on all 6 params (FLASH_ATTN/FLEX_ATTENTION/TRITON_ATTN x flex block\r\nshapes) both before and after this change; 417.50s -> 435.93s, i.e. the longer\r\nprompts add 4.4% to that test.\r\n\r\nNo model-quality impact is expected on CUDA: the source change is inside the XPU\r\nshim only, and the test change only lengthens prompts.\r\n\r\n🤖 Co-written with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 3,
